  "id": "behavioral-inhibition",
  "term": "behavioral inhibition",
  "definition": "Behavioral inhibition is a temperament pattern in which a child tends to be highly inhibited, and it is associated with greater risk for internalizing disorders. It may show up differently across contexts, so reports from different adults can give different pictures of the child’s behavior.",
